{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b2d0a5f4-894e-4a84-9b96-730ae3e46448","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A triangle has three vertices. We’ll connect each vertex to the midpoint of the opposite side and see where these lines meet.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Where do the medians meet?"},{"op":"figure","id":"triangle","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.7,6.7],"y":[-0.7,5.2],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[0,0],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[6,0],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","id":"c","at":[1.5,4.5],"label":"C"},{"kind":"polyline","points":[{"at":"a"},{"at":"b"},{"at":"c"}],"closed":true}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b2d0a5f4-894e-4a84-9b96-730ae3e46448","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Mark the midpoint of side BC. The segment from A to this midpoint is called a median.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"first_median","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"m","at":{"mid":["b","c"]},"label":"M"},{"kind":"segment","id":"median_a","from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"m"}},{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"m"},"label":"d"},{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"m"},"to":{"at":"c"},"label":"d"}]},{"op":"text","id":"definition","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Median: vertex to opposite midpoint"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b2d0a5f4-894e-4a84-9b96-730ae3e46448","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Now draw the median from B. It crosses the first median at a point we’ll call G.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"second_median","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"n","at":{"mid":["a","c"]},"label":"N"},{"kind":"segment","id":"median_b","from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"n"}},{"kind":"point","id":"g","at":{"hit":["median_a","median_b"]},"label":"G"}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Where on side AB should the median from C end?","expected_gist":"At the midpoint of AB."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b2d0a5f4-894e-4a84-9b96-730ae3e46448","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The third median passes through G too. All three medians meet at this single point, called the centroid.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"third_median","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":{"mid":["a","b"]},"label":"P"},{"kind":"segment","id":"median_c","from":{"at":"c"},"to":{"at":"p"}},{"kind":"text","at":[3.45,1.5],"text":"centroid","size":"small"},{"kind":"segment","from":[3.3,1.5],"to":{"at":"g"},"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"text","id":"conclusion","anchor":{"el":"definition","side":"below","gap":0.12},"content":"Three medians meet at one centroid."}],"checkpoint":null}}
